// response is the domain, as in GET /domains/{id}. Reply tracking: each tracked email gets its own
// signed Reply-To, e.g. r1-<email id>.<signature>@reply.acme.com, so replies come back tied to the
// exact email. Each reply fires email.replied (classified as a person, out-of-office, unsubscribe
// request, bounce…) and arrives as a received email; only replies a person wrote are forwarded. The
// display name is kept (the Reply-To’s name, else the From name). One reply address takes at most 100
// replies a day.
